Customer Stories.

Why the needles matter ? 

1. Slide: (Progressive) For example, the stakeholders at this insurance company who were responsible for delivering a new quoting system that needed to be reliable in all 50 states. They struggled to find needles in the haystack because the needles weren’t showing up on any dashboards.  

In most customer monitoring scenarios, this is commonplace as we often monitor based on size of customer or traffic.

While  company does business in all 50 states most of thier traffic comes from East Coast USA. Since with SPlunk APM you have ALL traces retained, the cusotmer was able to bucket their traffic by state, and find out that Hawaii was the state with issues at that time. 

Flash Sale Shoes ! 

2. Slide : Customer has flash sales that are very revenue generating and the architects owned the audit of complex checkout logic for these sales.

Since the traffic was so large, the could not find individual issues. However with splunk,  Being able to filter down to the specific workflow relative to the new mobile release is how they got a clear 
understanding of what was happening, why it was happening and therefore improve downtime. 

The custom tag in this case was “app-checkout” but we see “customer ID” used for retailers as well, or “policy-type or quote-type” for insurance or even “card type” for Finserv.

3. The Payment services at a large customer had very complex business logic.  Think: sales tax with multiple shipping addresses, gift cards, credit cards, etc.  Everytime someone would complain they weren’t charged the right price they spent over 90 minutes just stitching together logs to figure out how the business logic played out. 

The solution was Full Fidelity Distributed tracing with Splunk, why  ? First, we gave them the ability to understand the business Logic and how it was executing, to ensure what was or wasnt charged.


